ROLE: novelty_killer  VOTE: red

CLOSEST_PRIOR_WORK:
- {cite: "ArkVale: Efficient Generative LLM Inference with Recallable Key-Value Eviction (Chen et al., NeurIPS 2024)", url: "https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2024 ; openreview id 4oAt5L4lYe ; github.com/pku-liang/ArkVale", why_close: "Explicitly evicts KV then RECALLS pages that become important later via key-geometry digests — i.e. it already solves the exact 'cold-then-hot delayed callback' problem CLAIM-0010 claims to own, and does so WITHOUT any lexical handle signal."}
- {cite: "Learning to Evict from Key-Value Cache / KV Policy (Moschella, Manduchi, Sener — Apple, arXiv:2602.10238, Feb 2026)", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.10238 ; ADS 2026arXiv260210238M ; machinelearning.apple.com/research/evict", why_close: "Identical motivating framing — 'recency and past-attention are only INDIRECT proxies for a token's FUTURE value' — and learns future usefulness directly. This is CLAIM-0010's entire conceptual thesis, already published."}
- {cite: "A2SF: Accumulative Attention Scoring with Forgetting Factor (Jo & Shin, arXiv:2407.20485)", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.20485", why_close: "Owns the 'accumulated attention is a biased importance signal → decay it with a forgetting factor' diagnosis. CLAIM-0010's 'decayed past-attention' proxy IS A2SF's discounted accumulated attention."}
- {cite: "H2O: Heavy-Hitter Oracle (Zhang et al., arXiv:2306.14048, NeurIPS 2023); SnapKV (Li et al., arXiv:2404.14469); Quest (arXiv:2406.10774); InfiniGen (arXiv:2406.19707); Scissorhands (arXiv:2305.17118)", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.14048", why_close: "Stated baselines + the persistence-of-importance hypothesis the claim contests — and which the L1 data CONFIRMS rather than refutes."}

NAMING_VS_MECHANISM: Almost entirely renaming. The two load-bearing mechanism components are both subsumed: (1) the decayed/accumulated past-attention proxy = A2SF + H2O; (2) the "predict future re-reference, don't trust past-attention, recall spans that go hot later" framing = Apple-KVP + ArkVale. The ONLY component with no exact prior art (independently verified — no match across arXiv/NeurIPS/OpenReview for lexical-recurrence-as-eviction-importance on tool-result spans) is the lexical/n-gram handle-recurrence signal. But that residual is a naming-level differentiator on a thin feature, and the L1 shows it is empirically inert.

FATAL_COLLISIONS:
- ArkVale (≥2 sources: NeurIPS proceedings hash cd4b49379…, OpenReview 4oAt5L4lYe, github.com/pku-liang/ArkVale) — already does evict-then-recall on cold-then-hot spans without a lexical signal, which is the claim's purported gap.
- Apple "Learning to Evict" (≥2 independent indices: arXiv:2602.10238, ADS bibcode 2026arXiv260210238M, machinelearning.apple.com) — the suspicious-looking ID was independently confirmed REAL (2602 = Feb 2026); it pre-states the claim's framing.
- A2SF + H2O (≥2 sources, both retrievable) — jointly own the entire attention-proxy half of the predictor.

MANDATORY_RELATED_WORK: ArkVale; Apple "Learning to Evict from KV Cache" (KVP); A2SF; H2O; SnapKV; Quest; InfiniGen; Scissorhands. Plus, to defend the lexical-reuse distinction, the authors would have to distinguish KVShare (arXiv:2503.16525), LMCache, RadixAttention/vLLM prefix caching, Continuum (arXiv:2511.02230), and KVFlow — none of which use lexical recurrence as a retention-importance score, but all of which are adjacent.

RATIONALE: Independent prior-art search (verified ≥2 sources per fatal collision) confirms the claim's mechanism is already covered: the attention-decay proxy by A2SF/H2O (2407.20485, 2306.14048), and the "future-value over past-attention, recall-when-hot" thesis by Apple-KVP (2602.10238, ID confirmed genuine) and ArkVale (NeurIPS24). The single surviving novel feature — lexical handle-recurrence on tool-result spans — is moot, not merely thin: the L1 (806 real Qwen2.5-1.5B spans, pre-registered) measures lexical-proxy future-ref AUC = 0.857/0.647, STRICTLY WEAKER than H2O's 0.999/0.819 (1.000 on the critical handle), and CAUSAL−H2O pass@1 = +0.00 [CI 0,0] at every budget because H2O already ranks the handle #1. The cold-then-hot premise that would have given the lexical signal something to do occurs at 0.000 frequency. So the only non-renamed component delivers zero measured advantage over an existing baseline. Empirical refutation + mechanism subsumption ⇒ red/kill.
